You could search for a number of mouse related plugins. With a quick google:
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/triacontane/RPGMakerMV/master/PictureCallCommon.js
Mouse System Ex
Introduction  TDDP – MouseSystemEx lets you set and change custom mouse cursors during gameplay and event interaction; enables mouse interaction to trigger events without the player character; show icons next to the mouse, and much more.  Before asking for help, please read the documentation...
forums.rpgmakerweb.com
But I think for hover you can also just store the coordinates without the click in the mouse method (copy paste to notepad, save as .js file and add as a plugin). Then you can check TouchInput._hoverX and TouchInput._hoverY in a script. And for click you can check TouchInput.x and TouchInput.y
TouchInput._onMouseMove = function(event) {
if (this._mousePressed) {
var x = Graphics.pageToCanvasX(event.pageX);
var y = Graphics.pageToCanvasY(event.pageY);
this._onMove(x, y);
}
this._hoverX = Graphics.pageToCanvasX(event.pageX);
this._hoverY = Graphics.pageToCanvasY(event.pageY);
};
